Hades is a distilled harness. Its direct ancestor is Hermes Agent, and its design is a conscious reduction
of that harness: the tool loop, skills, session shape, gateway and memory seam, rebuilt in Rust with
explicit permissions and an evidence trail. The terminal coding-agent pattern it follows was made familiar
by Claude Code and the Codex CLI; Hades wraps neither and runs its own loop. It also builds on Linux
Landlock for isolation and SQLite FTS5 for memory. These are design influences and foundations, not
affiliations.

The upstream Hermes Agent Python source is the reference the Rust runtime was ported from. It is not
included in this release checkout and is not built, installed, or run by anything under rust/. The four
Rust crates (harness, session-tree, mneme, governance) are new work; session-tree, mneme and governance
were ported from that Python specification and are covered by parity oracles.

